# Agent worktrees. `git worktree` checkouts live inside the project root, so a
# reflexive `git add -A` would stage four full copies of the repository. They are
# also why `vite.config.ts` excludes them from the test gate — Vitest was
# collecting every copy's suite and reporting 755 passing tests for a suite of
# 151 (BAR-171).
.claude/worktrees/

# Working scratch, not deliverables
*.log

# The BOA "Ritual" brand system — 40 MB of poster and band artwork, including
# unannounced 2026 lineup images. Not a project contract: per ADR-009 the app
# design file governs every app-surface value, and the app itself loads only
# public/assets/. Its text tokens and guideline cards are preserved in
# references/brand-tokens/ because the docs reference them.
Bangalore Open Air — Ritual/

# Deliberately TRACKED, listed here so nobody adds them by reflex:
#   references/design-source/   the recovered design and spec — the UI contract
#   references/ui/              screen-keyed reference captures (acceptance artefacts)
#   references/brand-tokens/    brand text tokens (ADR-009 scope)
#   audit-current/              reference and implementation captures
#   BOA-Bar.html                the original bundled design artifact
#   BOA_Bar_Inventory.pptx      the approved slide deck
#   Bar Inventory.docx          the original written specification
# These are large binaries, but they are the project's contracts. Losing them is
# how this project spent five weeks building against assumptions — see
# docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-001. If repository size becomes a problem, move them to
# Git LFS; do not untrack them.
.vercel
